ptide  following the signal peptide we see a  pro-peptide sequence  which has no functional constraints and  as such  seems to have mostly stereochemical ones  such as proline in position 21  we see that the pro peptide sequence is  strongly biased towards negatively  charged amino acids  aspartic acid and glutamic acid these  are here to stabilize positively charged  mature defensing when it assembles  notably  we see that cysteines important for  stability of the cleave defensin  still remain highly favorable for each  position in the sequence  we have the presence probability of each  of the 20 natural amino acids displayed  as a heat map  it can also be visualized as a bar plot  another way to leverage the power of  these language models is with our  sequence generation tool  by selecting one or more positions in  the sequence as mutable  we can then generate most probable  variants  this slider here allows me to adjust the  number of generated sequences  that's it we've seen how to get insights  on protein sequences  using state-of-the-art machine learning  models and deep chains playground  thank you for watching and enjoy deep  chain
 

